<!-- ══════════ Section 5 ══════════ -->
<span class="section-num">5.</span>
<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew § 5</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה בְּחִינַת כְּבוֹד רַבּוֹ שֶׁגָּדוֹל מִכְּבוֹד אָבִיו, כְּמוֹ שֶׁאָמְרוּ רַבּוֹתֵינוּ זַ"ל, אֲבֵדַת רַבּוֹ וַאֲבֵדַת אָבִיו, אֲבֵדַת רַבּוֹ קוֹדֶמֶת, שֶׁאָבִיו מְבִיאוֹ לְחַיֵּי עוֹלָם הַזֶּה וְרַבּוֹ מְבִיאוֹ לְחַיֵּי עוֹלָם הַבָּא. כִּי עִקַּר כִּבּוּד אָב הוּא בִּשְׁבִיל לְהוֹצִיא אֶת הַכָּבוֹד מִזִּילוּתָא דְּגָלוּתָא וּלְהַפְשִׁיט נַפְשׁוֹ מִבְּגָדִים הַצּוֹאִים, וּלְהַלְבִּישׁ הַנֶּפֶשׁ בִּבְגָדִים נְקִיִּים בְּבִגְדֵי כָּבוֹד, שֶׁזֶּה נַעֲשֶׂה עַל-יְדֵי הַעֲלָאַת הַכָּבוֹד לְשָׁרְשׁוֹ, עַל-יְדֵי כִּבּוּד אָב וָאֵם, עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁמַּחֲזִיר הַכָּבוֹד לְאָבִיו וְאִמּוֹ שֶׁהִמְשִׁיכוּ נִשְׁמָתוֹ בָּעוֹלָם אֲשֶׁר שָׁרְשָׁהּ בַּכָּבוֹד וְכוּ' וְכַנַּ"ל. וְעַל-כֵּן כְּבוֹד רַבּוֹ גָּדוֹל מִזֶּה, כִּי עִקַּר שֹׁרֶשׁ הַנְּפָשׁוֹת בְּשָׁרְשָׁן הֵם נִמְשָׁכִין עַל-יְדֵי רַבּוֹ שֶׁלִּמְּדוֹ תּוֹרָה, כִּי הַתּוֹרָה הִוא שִׁשִּׁים רִבּוֹא אוֹתִיּוֹת כְּנֶגֶד שִׁשִּׁים רִבּוֹא נִשְׁמוֹת יִשְׂרָאֵל שֶׁהֵם כְּלַל כָּל הַנְּשָׁמוֹת וְכַמְבֹאָר בַּמַּאֲמָר הַנַּ"ל, שֶׁעִקַּר כְּבוֹד ה' יִתְבָּרַךְ, דְּהַיְנוּ לְהַחֲזִיר בְּנֵי אָדָם בִּתְשׁוּבָה הוּא עַל-יְדֵי עֵסֶק הַתּוֹרָה בִּקְדֻשָּׁה עַד שֶׁיְּעוֹרֵר עַל-יְדֵי הַתּוֹרָה שָׁרְשֵׁי הַנְּשָׁמוֹת וְכוּ', עַיֵּן שָׁם. נִמְצָא שֶׁעִקַּר הַכָּבוֹד נִתְהַוֶּה עַל-יְדֵי רַבּוֹ הָעוֹסֵק בַּתּוֹרָה, עַל-כֵּן שָׁם שֹׁרֶשׁ הַכָּבוֹד, עַל-כֵּן מְחֻיָּב לְכַבְּדוֹ, כִּי שָׁם שֹׁרֶשׁ הַכָּבוֹד כַּנַּ"ל. וּכְבוֹדוֹ יוֹתֵר מִכְּבוֹד אָבִיו, כִּי הָרַב מְעוֹרֵר הַכָּבוֹד בְּשָׁרְשׁוֹ עַל-יְדֵי עֵסֶק הַתּוֹרָה שֶׁהִיא שָׁרְשֵׁי נִשְׁמוֹת יִשְׂרָאֵל וְכַנַּ"ל:</div>

<p class="first">And this is the aspect of <strong>the honor of one's Rav, which is greater than the honor of his father</strong>. As our Sages of blessed memory said: <span class="verse-inline">"The lost object of his Rav and the lost object of his father — the lost object of his Rav takes precedence, for his father brings him to the life of this world, and his Rav brings him to the life of the World to Come."</span></p>

<p>For the primary <em>kibud av</em> is in order to extract the <em>kavod</em> from the degradation of exile, and to strip from his <em>nefesh</em> the soiled garments, and to clothe the <em>nefesh</em> in clean garments, in garments of <em>kavod</em>. And this is accomplished through raising the <em>kavod</em> to its root, through <em>kibud av va'aim</em> — through returning the <em>kavod</em> to his father and mother, who drew his <em>neshamah</em> into the world, whose root is in the <em>kavod</em> etc., as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And therefore the honor of one's Rav is greater than this. For the primary root of the <em>nefashos</em> at their source — they are drawn through his Rav who taught him Torah. For the Torah has 600,000 letters corresponding to the 600,000 <em>neshamos</em> of Israel, which are the totality of all the <em>neshamos</em>, as is explained in the aforementioned <em>ma'amar</em>: that the primary <em>kavod</em> of Hashem, blessed be He — that is, to bring people back in <em>teshuvah</em> — is through engaging in Torah in holiness, until he awakens through the Torah the roots of the <em>neshamos</em> etc.; see there.</p>

<p>It turns out that the primary <em>kavod</em> comes into being through his Rav, who engages in the Torah. Therefore there is the root of the <em>kavod</em>; therefore one is obligated to honor him, for there is the root of the <em>kavod</em>, as mentioned above. And his honor is greater than the honor of his father, for the Rav awakens the <em>kavod</em> at its root — through engaging in Torah, which is the root of the <em>neshamos</em> of Israel, as mentioned above.</p>

<!-- ══════════ Section 6 ══════════ -->
<span class="section-num">6.</span>
<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew § 6</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְעַל-כֵּן אִיתָא, שֶׁרַב מְפֻרְסָם וְגָדוֹל בְּדוֹרוֹ דִּינוֹ כְּרַב מֻבְהָק אַף-עַל-פִּי שֶׁלֹּא קִבֵּל מִמֶּנּוּ כְּלוּם, כִּי רַב מְפֻרְסָם, הַיְנוּ צַדִּיק הַדּוֹר הָאֱמֶת שֶׁעוֹסֵק בַּתּוֹרָה בִּקְדֻשָּׁה גְּדוֹלָה עַד שֶׁהוּא מְעוֹרֵר עַל-יְדֵי עֵסֶק הַתּוֹרָה שֶׁלּוֹ שָׁרְשֵׁי הַנְּשָׁמוֹת. עַד שֶׁמַּגִּיעַ עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה הֶאָרָה אֲפִלּוּ לְהָרְחוֹקִים מִמֶּנּוּ חֲמִשִּׁים פַּרְסָאוֹת וְחוֹזְרִים בִּתְשׁוּבָה שֶׁזֶּה עִקַּר כְּבוֹדוֹ יִתְבָּרַךְ. נִמְצָא, שֶׁהַצַּדִּיק הָאֱמֶת שֶׁבַּדּוֹר הוּא הָרַב שֶׁל כָּל הַדּוֹר כֻּלּוֹ, אֲפִלּוּ שֶׁל אוֹתָן הָרְחוֹקִים מִמֶּנּוּ מְאֹד, אַף-עַל-פִּי שֶׁלֹּא קִבְּלוּ מִמֶּנּוּ שׁוּם דָּבָר, כִּי עַל-יְדֵי עֵסֶק תּוֹרָתוֹ מְעוֹרֵר כָּל הָעוֹלָם בִּתְשׁוּבָה. וְעַל-כֵּן הָרַב הַמְפֻרְסָם, הַיְנוּ הַצַּדִּיק הָאֱמֶת שֶׁבַּדּוֹר, דִּינוֹ כְּרַב מֻבְהָק לְכָל הָעוֹלָם כֻּלּוֹ וְהַכֹּל חַיָּבִים בִּכְבוֹדוֹ. כִּי הוּא רַבָּם מַמָּשׁ שֶׁל כָּל הָעוֹלָם, כִּי הוּא מְעוֹרֵר בִּתְשׁוּבָה כָּל בְּנֵי עוֹלָם עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁהוּא שֹׁרֶשׁ נִשְׁמוֹת יִשְׂרָאֵל וְכוּ' כַּנַּ"ל. וְעַל-כֵּן מְחֻיָּבִים לְכַבְּדוֹ בְּיוֹתֵר, כִּי עִקַּר כָּל הַכָּבוֹד עַל יָדוֹ עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁמַּחֲזִיר בְּנֵי אָדָם בִּתְשׁוּבָה עַל-יְדֵי תּוֹרָתוֹ שֶׁזֶּה עִקַּר כְּבוֹדוֹ וְכוּ' וְכַנַּ"ל:</div>

<p class="first">And therefore it is brought that <strong>a Rav who is famous and great in his generation has the status of a <em>Rav muvhak</em></strong> <span class="added">[primary teacher]</span> even though one did not receive anything from him. For a famous Rav — that is, the true <em>tzadik</em> of the generation — who engages in Torah with such great holiness that he awakens through his Torah study the roots of the <em>neshamos</em>, until through this illumination reaches even those who are fifty <em>parsa'os</em> <span class="added">[a great distance]</span> from him, and they return in <em>teshuvah</em> — this is the primary glory of Hashem, blessed be He.</p>

<p>It turns out that the true <em>tzadik</em> of the generation is the Rav of the entire generation — even of those who are very far from him, even though they did not receive any teaching from him. For through engaging in his Torah he awakens the entire world in <em>teshuvah</em>.</p>

<p>And therefore the famous Rav — that is, the true <em>tzadik</em> of the generation — has the status of a <em>Rav muvhak</em> to the entire world. And everyone is obligated in his honor. For he is literally their Rav, of the entire world — for he awakens in <em>teshuvah</em> all the people of the world, through his being the root of the <em>neshamos</em> of Israel etc., as mentioned above. And therefore one is obligated to honor him greatly, for the primary <em>kavod</em> comes through him — through his bringing people back in <em>teshuvah</em> through his Torah. And this is the primary <em>kavod</em> etc., as mentioned above.</p>

